<title>USA: Harcourt offers $14/shr for Steck-Vaughn.</title>
<headline>Harcourt offers $14/shr for Steck-Vaughn.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Publishing company Harcourt General Inc said Tuesday it had offered to buy stock of Steck Vaughn Publishing Corp that it does not already own for $14 per share, or $36.4 million.</p>
<p>Harcourt already owns about 82 percent of Steck-Vaughn following its recently-completed acquisition of National Education Corp.  </p>
<p>Harcourt and Steck-Vaughn also announced that they have changed the Steck-Vaughn's board of directors to reflect Harcourt's ownership position.  The Steck-Vaughn board now includes four Harcourt executives, as well as four independent directors.</p>
<p>Under an agreement between the two companies, the Harcourt offer will be reviewed by the independent directors.</p>
<p>Steck-Vaughn shares rose 5/8 to 14-1/8 in early trading.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk, 212/859-1700))</p>
